{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a partial-capacity disability benefit for those reducing work hours",
        "additional_details": "The UK benefits system can trap workers with chronic illnesses like fibromyalgia. Many can do daily tasks independently, making them ineligible for PIP. Yet, full-time work can cause severe pain and exhaustion. When occupational health advises reducing hours, they face a major pay cut. Means-tested benefits like Universal Credit are blocked if a partner earns well, leaving them trapped. We believe workers shouldn't have to break their bodies to pay bills - we need a financial bridge to support partial hours.",
        "background": "We want the Government to introduce a ongoing disability benefit to top up the income of working individuals with chronic illnesses who need to reduce their hours on medical advice, without facing financial hardship.",
